      "head_commit": {
        "id": "a2a628f4fd5aa33da99fb3a41e7070b579eaf540",
        "tree_id": "c82cb752b88bfbaf94696729c622c6d9963815ab",
        "message": "feat(mcp): speak the 2026-07-28 revision, keep legacy clients working\n\nResearched the current spec and it moved on from what was implemented:\nMCP 2026-07-28 is stateless. Protocol-level sessions and the\nMcp-Session-Id header are gone, the initialize/notifications/initialized\nhandshake is gone, the GET stream endpoint is gone, and every request now\ncarries its version and client capabilities in _meta.\n\nServer is now dual-era on the same endpoint:\n\nModern (2026-07-28)\n- Stateless dispatch; no initialize, no session.\n- Requires MCP-Protocol-Version and validates it against\n  _meta.io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion (400 HeaderMismatch,\n  -32020), rejects unknown versions with UnsupportedProtocolVersionError\n  (-32022) listing what we support, and rejects requests missing the\n  required _meta fields (400, -32602).\n- Implements server/discover (MUST in this revision).\n- Results carry resultType:\"complete\" and a _meta serverInfo block;\n  list results carry the required ttlMs/cacheScope.\n- Unknown RPC -> 404 + -32601; notifications -> 202 with no body.\n- Validates the Origin header to block DNS rebinding, and sets\n  X-Accel-Buffering: no on SSE replies.\n\nLegacy (2025-11-25 and earlier)\n- initialize handshake, ping, logging/setLevel kept, plus the deprecated\n  HTTP+SSE transport, so older clients still connect.\n\nAlso: the MCP settings screen now reads in Chinese (values-zh-rCN was\nmissing all 24 new strings), and the docs describe the dual-era support.",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-11T08:28:22Z",
